IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hprnl-dates`

-- Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Victoria) Act 2009 -- the whole Act, as the HEALTH PRACTITIONER meets it.
--
-- SEAT: the person to whom the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law is applied in Victoria: a registered health
-- practitioner, an applicant for registration or a student, and in particular the person who is the subject of an
-- appellable decision. "Does the National Law apply to me as a law of Victoria?", "Where will my matter be heard?",
-- "Can I still apply to VCAT to review the decision about me, and by when?", "Can I rely on this Victorian Act in my
-- dealings under the National Law?". A person who made a notification about a practitioner (for example a patient) may
-- ask the last question too. The National Boards, the national agency, VCAT and the courts get no seat.
--
-- The Act is short: it adopts the National Law (the Schedule to the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law Act 2009
-- of Queensland), which is NOT in the deposited text. Terms the Act borrows from that Law ("appellable decision",
-- "responsible tribunal") are asked as facts.
--
-- Every exported question takes plain facts (yes/no, dates, a choice from a list). The 28-day limits of ss 6A(2) and
-- 9(2) are a DEONTIC rule run inside; no question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Health
-- Practitioner Regulation National Law (Victoria) Act 2009, Act No. 79/2009, Version No. 006 (31 May 2019), not the
-- authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with the authority of the Government Printer for the State of
-- Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's
-- ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Victoria): the practitioner's questions`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 2, 4 -- the National Law as a law of Victoria`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 2 "This Act comes into operation on 1 July 2010."
`the day this Act came into operation` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 7 2010

-- s 4 "The Health Practitioner Regulation National Law, as in force from time to time, set out in the Schedule to the
-- Health Practitioner Regulation National Law Act 2009 of Queensland-- (a) applies as a law of Victoria; and (b) as so
-- applying may be referred to as the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Victoria); and (c) so applies as if
-- it were part of this Act."
-- JUST TRUE from 1 July 2010; JUST FALSE before it (s 2 fixes the day in its own words: periods ruling (a)).
GIVEN `the day asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 2, 4 -- the National Law applies as a law of Victoria` `the day asked` MEANS
    IF `the day` `the day asked` `is before` `the day this Act came into operation`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@export Does the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law apply to me as a law of Victoria on a given day (Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Victoria) Act 2009 ss 2, 4)? From 1 July 2010 the National Law, as in force from time to time (it is set out in the Schedule to a Queensland Act), applies as a law of Victoria, is called the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Victoria), and applies as if it were part of the Victorian Act. Before 1 July 2010 it did not.
GIVEN `the day asked` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (ISO date, for example 2026-11-07)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the National Law apply to me in Victoria` MEANS
    `ss 2, 4 -- the National Law applies as a law of Victoria` `the day asked`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 5, 6 -- where my matter is heard`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 6 "VCAT is declared to be the responsible tribunal for this jurisdiction for the purposes of the Health Practitioner
-- Regulation National Law (Victoria)." s 5 "magistrate means a magistrate within the meaning of the Magistrates' Court
-- Act 1989; magistrates' court means the Magistrates' Court of Victoria. this jurisdiction means Victoria." Which matters
-- the National Law gives to the responsible tribunal or to a magistrate is in the National Law, not deposited: asked.
DECLARE `Kind of matter` IS ONE OF
    `a matter the National Law gives to the responsible tribunal`
    `a matter the National Law gives to a magistrate or a magistrates' court`
    `another matter`

DECLARE `Where my matter is heard` IS ONE OF
    `VCAT (the Victorian Civil and Administrative Tribunal), the responsible tribunal for Victoria (s 6)`
    `a magistrate within the meaning of the Magistrates' Court Act 1989, or the Magistrates' Court of Victoria (s 5)`
    `not covered: this Act names no court or tribunal for this matter`
    `not covered: the National Law did not apply in Victoria before 1 July 2010 (s 2)`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of matter`, `the day asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Where my matter is heard`
`ss 5, 6 -- the Victorian forum` `the kind` `the day asked` MEANS
    IF `the day` `the day asked` `is before` `the day this Act came into operation`
    THEN `not covered: the National Law did not apply in Victoria before 1 July 2010 (s 2)`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the kind`
         WHEN `a matter the National Law gives to the responsible tribunal` THEN `VCAT (the Victorian Civil and Administrative Tribunal), the responsible tribunal for Victoria (s 6)`
         WHEN `a matter the National Law gives to a magistrate or a magistrates' court` THEN `a magistrate within the meaning of the Magistrates' Court Act 1989, or the Magistrates' Court of Victoria (s 5)`
         OTHERWISE `not covered: this Act names no court or tribunal for this matter`

@export In Victoria, which tribunal or court hears my matter under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Victoria) Act 2009 ss 5, 6)? Where the National Law sends a matter to "the responsible tribunal" (for example an appeal against an appellable decision), in Victoria that is VCAT; where it sends a matter to a magistrate or a magistrates' court, it is a Victorian magistrate or the Magistrates' Court of Victoria.
GIVEN `the kind of matter` IS A `Kind of matter` @desc What the National Law says about your matter: it goes to the responsible tribunal (for example your appeal against an appellable decision, or a matter a National Board refers to a tribunal); it goes to a magistrate or a magistrates' court; or another matter
      `the day asked` IS A DATE @desc The day the matter is, or is to be, heard or started (ISO date)
GIVETH A `Where my matter is heard`
`Where will my matter be heard` MEANS
    `ss 5, 6 -- the Victorian forum` `the kind of matter` `the day asked`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 6A, 9 -- applying to VCAT to review an appellable decision about me (arises only if such a decision is made)`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 6A(1) "A person who is the subject of an appellable decision under section 199 of the Health Practitioner
-- Regulation National Law (Victoria) may appeal against that decision by lodging an application for review of that
-- decision by VCAT." (2) "An application under subsection (1) must be lodged no more than 28 days after the person has
-- been given notice of the appellable decision."
-- s 9(1) "Section 6A applies to an application lodged on or after 1 July 2012." (2) "If an appellable decision is made
-- before 1 July 2012, an application for review of that appellable decision must be lodged with VCAT no more than 28
-- days after 1 July 2012."
`the day s 6A began to apply` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 7 2012

`the days allowed to lodge` MEANS 28

-- The limit as a rule with a deadline, counted in days from the day the 28 days run from (day 0: the day notice was
-- given under s 6A(2), or 1 July 2012 under s 9(2)). "No more than 28 days after" day 0 lets the application be lodged
-- on day 28 and not on day 29 (fork F1). Missing the deadline is not a wrong done by the person; the BREACH marks only
-- that the limit was not met (VCAT may extend it: NOTES.md, finding 3).
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF `I`
DECLARE `Act done` IS ONE OF `lodge an application for review by VCAT`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act done`
`ss 6A(2), 9(2) -- lodge within the days allowed` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `I`
    DO `lodge an application for review by VCAT`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `I` BECAUSE "the application for review was not lodged with VCAT within the 28 days the Act allows (s 6A(2) or s 9(2))"

-- The helper that runs the rule over what happened (as in the Victims of Crime, County Court and Legal Profession
-- Uniform Law encodings). On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH. It takes a
-- DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Party` `Act done`
      `the time it was done` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `lodged in time under` `the rule` `at` `the time it was done` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time it was done`), (EVENT `I` `lodge an application for review by VCAT` `the time it was done`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `My application to VCAT` IS ONE OF
    `not covered: s 6A gives me no appeal, because I am not the subject of an appellable decision under s 199 of the National Law`
    `not covered: the National Law did not apply in Victoria before 1 July 2010 (s 2), so no appellable decision under it was made`
    `not covered: s 6A does not apply to an application lodged before 1 July 2012 (s 9(1)); its time limit is outside this Act`
    `yes, in time: I may apply to VCAT for review; the 28 days have not begun, because I have not yet been given notice of the decision (s 6A)`
    `yes, in time: I may apply to VCAT for review, no more than 28 days after I was given notice of the decision (s 6A)`
    `no, out of time: more than 28 days after I was given notice of the decision (s 6A(2)); VCAT may extend the time (VCAT Act s 126)`
    `yes, in time: the decision was made before 1 July 2012, and I lodge no more than 28 days after 1 July 2012 (s 9(2))`
    `no, out of time: the decision was made before 1 July 2012, and I lodge more than 28 days after 1 July 2012 (s 9(2)); VCAT may extend the time (VCAT Act s 126)`

-- Fork F2: for a decision made before 1 July 2012, s 9(2) alone sets the limit (it is the specific rule); the other
-- reading applies s 6A(2) as well and takes the earlier day. Fork F3: before notice is given, the 28 days of s 6A(2)
-- have not begun and an application is in time; the other reading: no application can be lodged before notice.
GIVEN `appellable decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am its subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was made` IS A DATE
      `notice given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of notice` IS A DATE
      `the day lodged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `My application to VCAT`
`ss 6A, 9 -- my application to VCAT` `appellable decision` `I am its subject` `the day it was made` `notice given` `the day of notice` `the day lodged` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`appellable decision` AND `I am its subject`)
        THEN `not covered: s 6A gives me no appeal, because I am not the subject of an appellable decision under s 199 of the National Law`
        IF `the day` `the day it was made` `is before` `the day this Act came into operation`
        THEN `not covered: the National Law did not apply in Victoria before 1 July 2010 (s 2), so no appellable decision under it was made`
        IF `the day` `the day lodged` `is before` `the day s 6A began to apply`
        THEN `not covered: s 6A does not apply to an application lodged before 1 July 2012 (s 9(1)); its time limit is outside this Act`
        IF `the day` `the day it was made` `is before` `the day s 6A began to apply`
        THEN IF `lodged in time under` (`ss 6A(2), 9(2) -- lodge within the days allowed` `the days allowed to lodge`) `at` (`the days from` `the day s 6A began to apply` `to` `the day lodged`)
             THEN `yes, in time: the decision was made before 1 July 2012, and I lodge no more than 28 days after 1 July 2012 (s 9(2))`
             ELSE `no, out of time: the decision was made before 1 July 2012, and I lodge more than 28 days after 1 July 2012 (s 9(2)); VCAT may extend the time (VCAT Act s 126)`
        IF (NOT `notice given`) OR (`the day` `the day lodged` `is before` `the day of notice`)
        THEN `yes, in time: I may apply to VCAT for review; the 28 days have not begun, because I have not yet been given notice of the decision (s 6A)`
        IF `lodged in time under` (`ss 6A(2), 9(2) -- lodge within the days allowed` `the days allowed to lodge`) `at` (`the days from` `the day of notice` `to` `the day lodged`)
        THEN `yes, in time: I may apply to VCAT for review, no more than 28 days after I was given notice of the decision (s 6A)`
        OTHERWISE `no, out of time: more than 28 days after I was given notice of the decision (s 6A(2)); VCAT may extend the time (VCAT Act s 126)`

@export Can I apply to VCAT to review an appellable decision made about me under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law, and am I in time (Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Victoria) Act 2009 ss 6A, 9)? If you are the subject of an appellable decision (under s 199 of the National Law, for example a National Board's refusal to register you or a condition imposed on your registration), you may appeal by lodging an application for review with VCAT no more than 28 days after you were given notice of the decision. For a decision made before 1 July 2012, the limit was 28 days after 1 July 2012. VCAT itself may extend a time limit (VCAT Act s 126), which this question does not decide.
GIVEN `appellable decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision is an appellable decision under section 199 of the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (for example a National Board's decision to refuse you registration, or to impose or change a condition on your registration)
      `I am the subject of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the person the decision is about (the subject of the decision)
      `day decision made` IS A DATE @desc The day the decision was made (ISO date)
      `notice given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been given notice of the decision
      `day notice given` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given notice of the decision (ISO date); if no notice has been given, any date
      `day lodged` IS A DATE @desc The day you lodged, or will lodge, your application for review with VCAT (ISO date)
GIVETH A `My application to VCAT`
`Can I apply to VCAT in time` MEANS
    `ss 6A, 9 -- my application to VCAT` `appellable decision` `I am the subject of it` `day decision made` `notice given` `day notice given` `day lodged`

-- The last day the Act allows: notice day plus 28 (s 6A(2)); 1 July 2012 plus 28, that is 29 July 2012, for a decision
-- made before 1 July 2012 (s 9(2), fork F2). NOTHING where s 6A gives no appeal, before the National Law applied, or
-- before notice is given (the 28 days have not begun).
GIVEN `appellable decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am its subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was made` IS A DATE
      `notice given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`ss 6A(2), 9(2) -- the last day to lodge` `appellable decision` `I am its subject` `the day it was made` `notice given` `the day of notice` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`appellable decision` AND `I am its subject`)
        THEN NOTHING
        IF `the day` `the day it was made` `is before` `the day this Act came into operation`
        THEN NOTHING
        IF `the day` `the day it was made` `is before` `the day s 6A began to apply`
        THEN JUST (`the date` `the days allowed to lodge` `days after` `the day s 6A began to apply`)
        IF `notice given`
        THEN JUST (`the date` `the days allowed to lodge` `days after` `the day of notice`)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@export By what day must I lodge my application to VCAT for review of an appellable decision about me (Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Victoria) Act 2009 ss 6A(2), 9(2))? The last day is 28 days after the day you were given notice of the decision; for a decision made before 1 July 2012 it was 29 July 2012. No day is given if the decision is not an appellable decision about you, or if you have not yet been given notice. VCAT may extend the time (VCAT Act s 126).
GIVEN `appellable decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision is an appellable decision under section 199 of the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (for example a National Board's decision to refuse you registration, or to impose or change a condition on your registration)
      `I am the subject of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the person the decision is about (the subject of the decision)
      `day decision made` IS A DATE @desc The day the decision was made (ISO date)
      `notice given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been given notice of the decision
      `day notice given` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given notice of the decision (ISO date); if no notice has been given, any date
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must I apply to VCAT` MEANS
    `ss 6A(2), 9(2) -- the last day to lodge` `appellable decision` `I am the subject of it` `day decision made` `notice given` `day notice given`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 7 -- Victorian Acts that do not apply to the National Law (Victoria)`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 7 "The following Acts of this jurisdiction do not apply to the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law
-- (Victoria) or to the instruments made under that Law-- (a) the Audit Act 1994; (b) the Financial Management Act 1994;
-- (c) the Freedom of Information Act 1982; (d) the Health Records Act 2001; [(e) repealed] (f) the Interpretation of
-- Legislation Act 1984; (g) the Ombudsman Act 1973; (ga) the Privacy and Data Protection Act 2014; (h) the Public
-- Administration Act 2004; [(i) repealed] (j) the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994."
-- A flat negative ("do not apply"): JUST FALSE for a listed Act (ruling N2). The list is not closed with "only" and the
-- Act says nothing of any other Victorian Act: NOTHING. The text as at 31 May 2019 is encoded; (ga) has been there since
-- 17 September 2014 and earlier versions are not.
DECLARE `Victorian Act` IS ONE OF
    `the Audit Act 1994`
    `the Financial Management Act 1994`
    `the Freedom of Information Act 1982`
    `the Health Records Act 2001`
    `the Interpretation of Legislation Act 1984`
    `the Ombudsman Act 1973`
    `the Privacy and Data Protection Act 2014`
    `the Public Administration Act 2004`
    `the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994`
    `another Victorian Act`

GIVEN `the Act` IS A `Victorian Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7 -- the Victorian Act applies to the National Law (Victoria)` `the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Act`
    WHEN `another Victorian Act` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

@export Does this Victorian Act apply to the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Victoria) and the instruments made under it, so that I can rely on it in my dealings under the National Law (Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Victoria) Act 2009 s 7)? The Audit Act 1994, the Financial Management Act 1994, the Freedom of Information Act 1982, the Health Records Act 2001, the Interpretation of Legislation Act 1984, the Ombudsman Act 1973, the Privacy and Data Protection Act 2014, the Public Administration Act 2004 and the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 do not apply (answer: false). The Act says nothing about any other Victorian Act (answer: none).
GIVEN `the Victorian Act` IS A `Victorian Act` @desc The Victorian Act you want to rely on: the Audit Act 1994; the Financial Management Act 1994; the Freedom of Information Act 1982; the Health Records Act 2001; the Interpretation of Legislation Act 1984; the Ombudsman Act 1973; the Privacy and Data Protection Act 2014; the Public Administration Act 2004; the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994; or another Victorian Act
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does this Victorian Act apply to the National Law in Victoria` MEANS
    `s 7 -- the Victorian Act applies to the National Law (Victoria)` `the Victorian Act`
